"answer": "Project Zenith is a new data analytics initiative launched by Alex, with Sarah Tan as the lead. The project kicked off on June 15th with an initial budget of $500,000 for Phase One, which was later adjusted to $550,000 due to unforeseen expenses, and eventually received executive approval for a total budget of $2 million. The team expanded in September with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture. Key milestones include a call for AI-driven data visualization ideas in July, the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype ahead of schedule, and a breakthrough in predictive analytics in Phase Two. A detailed report on Phase Two progress will be presented on November 20th, and feedback on the prototype is being sought until the end of November. Additionally, the compliance plan's budget was increased to $55,000. XY Newspaper's Kitamura has requested an interview to cover the project's full scope."
